title: The Manifesto Launch
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: campaign
view-if: manifesto_launched = 0
on-arrival: manifesto_launched = 1; month_actions += 1

= The Manifesto Launch

The manifesto is printed and the press conference is booked. Your speechwriters have two drafts of the launch speech.

We have [+ manifesto_planks +] firm commitments.

- @bold: A radical break with the post-war consensus.
- @cautious: A safe pair of hands.
- @easy_discard

@bold
on-arrival: economic_liberalism += 3; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent) if economic_liberalism >= 50; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent) if economic_liberalism >= 50; c1_con -= 2 if economic_liberalism < 45; c1_lib += 2 if economic_liberalism < 45; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent) if manifesto_planks >= 4; dry_dissent -= 6; wet_dissent += 5

The manifesto promises to restore the balance of power in industry and to roll back the frontiers of the state. [? if economic_liberalism >= 50 : The mood of the country matches it. ?][? if economic_liberalism < 45 : Swing voters find it alarming. ?]

@cautious
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 8; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); c1_lib -= 1; dry_dissent += 4

The launch stresses competence, lower taxes and order, and says little about the money supply. Labour's scare campaign has less to work with.
